{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"polonium-deceptive-antelope","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"Follow-up to the closed P1 bug rubied-nonvagrant-whimbrel (dd30-f10d-69f3-4c36), whose code fix is merged (13e2ea6decc9c62484f80034e28cb96c20448ea2): the three unescaped ${...} sites in infra/terraform/user_data.sh comments were reworded, `terraform plan` now exits 0, and a regression guard (scripts/check_templatefile_escapes.py) is wired into `make lint`. That satisfied the bug's DoD (AC1: `terraform plan` completes).\n\nDEFERRED DEPLOYMENT DECISION (out of the original bug's envelope):\nThe pending `terraform plan` recorded on rubied reports `Plan: 6 to add, 1 to change, 0 to destroy`:\n- 2 new CloudWatch alarms: `mcp_mem_abort` and `mcp_retire_cap`\n- in-place update of `aws_instance.gerrit` user_data\n- 4 new `rebar_secrets` SSM params for MCP client PATs\nThe three `import` blocks in the plan are already adopted as no-op.\n\nRunning `terraform apply` against prod touches infrastructure beyond the dd30 bug's blast radius and is an OPERATOR DECISION requiring explicit human approval. This ticket tracks that go/no-go apply decision; it must NOT be executed autonomously by an agent.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- An operator explicitly reviews the recorded plan (6 add / 1 change / 0 destroy) and approves or rejects the `terraform apply`.\n- If approved, the apply is performed by/with a human operator and the resulting state is recorded back on this ticket.","id":"f268-32ae-4ea9-42fb","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Operator decision: apply the terraform plan for user_data + MCP SSM params (blast radius exceeds dd30 envelope)"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788021805459937974,"uuid":"8e0bf7e6-03cd-4d0a-a36f-0acbf10a5caa"}